      "message": "It is relative to the time of the call (for example, a call `setKeyValidity(10)` will make the key expire in 10 seconds). The call can only be done by the key creator and currently there is no limit on the number of times it can be invoked (the second call would set the validity to the desired period from the moment of the call). Do you see any advantages in making this a one-time call function?",
